# Deep Technical Research Canvas: How KùzuDB Works

> **Version context:** The sources below include Kùzu’s developer docs updated **Oct 10, 2025**, and note significant packaging/behavior changes around **v0.11.x** (e.g., single-file on-disk format, extension distribution). ([Kuzu][1])

---

## 0. The mental model

Kùzu is best understood as an **embedded, disk-based, read-optimized graph DBMS** that is architected like a “modern analytical engine” (columnar + vectorized execution) but purpose-built for **property-graph pattern matching** and **multi-hop traversal**. It runs **in-process** (SQLite/DuckDB-style), not as a separate server daemon. ([CIDRDB][2])

Kùzu’s research/design center of gravity is:

* **Property graph model**, but **schema-first** (node/rel “tables” with typed properties). ([CIDRDB][2])
* **Columnar storage** for properties + **CSR-based adjacency (“join indices”)** for topology. ([CIDRDB][2])
* A **factorized, vectorized query processor** with specialized join/traversal operators (notably **ASP-Join**) designed to keep scans sequential and avoid intermediate blowups in graph pattern queries. ([CIDRDB][2])
* **Serializable ACID** transactions with **one writer + multiple readers**, implemented with **WAL** and checkpointing. ([Kuzu][3])

---

## 1. High-level architecture (modules + dataflow)

Kùzu follows a “classic DBMS pipeline” with explicit modules for parse → bind → plan → optimize → execute, plus storage/buffer/txn subsystems. ([Kuzu][4])

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  Q[Cypher text] --> P[Parser<br/>antlr4 Cypher.g4]
  P --> B[Binder<br/>semantic checks + name->ID binding<br/>rewrites]
  B --> L[Planner<br/>LogicalPlan (relational algebra ops)]
  L --> O[Optimizer<br/>rule transforms + join optimization]
  O --> X[Processor<br/>PhysicalPlan + pipeline scheduler]
  X --> E[Execution engine<br/>pipelines + morsel parallelism]
  E --> R[Results]
  subgraph Storage&Txn
    S[Storage manager<br/>columns + CSR lists + indices]
    BM[BufferManager<br/>page cache]
    T[Transaction manager<br/>WAL + serializable]
  end
  X --> S
  S --> BM
  X --> T
```

Key specifics from Kùzu’s own developer internals:

* **Parser**: parses into an antlr4 AST (Cypher grammar file `Cypher.g4`), then transforms to internal `Statement`. ([Kuzu][4])
* **Binder**: binds names (e.g., table names) to internal IDs; performs **semantic rewrites** to improve evaluation without changing meaning. ([Kuzu][4])
* **Planner → Optimizer**: produces and transforms a `LogicalPlan`. ([Kuzu][4])
* **Processor**: maps logical ops (SCAN/FILTER/JOIN/…) to **specific physical algorithms**; also schedules pipelines for **morsel-driven parallelism**. ([Kuzu][4])

