## 8. Extension system: dynamic capability loading

Kùzu has an extension API designed to load functionality at runtime and keep the core library smaller. ([Kuzu][8])

Important operational notes from the official extension docs:

* As of **v0.11.3**, Kùzu pre-installs and pre-loads four common extensions: `algo`, `fts`, `json`, `vector`. ([Kuzu][8])
* Kùzu “no longer provides an official extensions server”; older versions or non-preinstalled extensions require hosting a **local extension server**. ([Kuzu][8])
* Extensions are **scoped to a session**, so if they aren’t pre-loaded you must `LOAD` each new session. ([Kuzu][8])

The official docs list available extensions including: `algo`, `fts`, `httpfs`, `json`, `llm`, `neo4j`, `postgres`, `sqlite`, `vector`, plus cloud/lakehouse connectors. ([Kuzu][8])

